31:  "changed" events with refetch, computed by diffing the exported read
67:- Preserve the existing presentation concepts: the compact working-set card, the full last-response view, and the complete navigable conversation for Claude Code sessions.
130:  - each WebSocket subscriber has an event queue of 256; when it fills, the subscriber is sent `resync_required` and closed, never silently trimmed (§4.4);
169:| GET | `/api/v1/waiting` | `waiting`; `?scope=all` as above | read |
170:| GET | `/api/v1/sessions/{id}/screen?lines=n` | `session.screen` | read |
173:| GET | `/api/v1/sessions/{id}/last-response` | new: `session.last_response` | read |
230:  "type": "changed",
243:- `resync_required`: sent before the host closes a subscriber whose queue overflowed; the client reconnects and refetches everything.
267:Because the subscriber is registered on the frame thread before any later pass can bump `revision`, a metadata snapshot is taken on that thread with the revision it carries, and a content reply is stamped on that thread when the worker's version action lands (the same moment its `changed` would be emitted, so the event and the reply name one revision), no change can fall between a subscription and a snapshot. Several snapshots in flight are each reconciled against the buffer by their own revision; events that arrive during a refetch are reconciled the same way, which is why the client never clears its buffer until step 4. A resource named by an event the client has never seen is fetched. If `epoch` differs from the one the client holds (the host restarted), every cached item is stale and is refetched. There is no retained-event replay: a `resync_required` is the only answer to a gap, and events are never durable.
353:- **SwitchboardUI:** shared SwiftUI card, last-response, conversation, run-output, working-set, server selector and connection status views.
439:**A3 — Synchronization.** The read-model diff after every pass, the revision counter moving, `changed` and `removed` events for metadata and collections, the WebSocket with `hello`, subscribe-then-snapshot and reconciliation by revision on the client, epoch handling, `resync_required`. `ops` and the log-before-run path in `serve` (no commands yet, but the path is tested here). *Built 2026-10-12; see design.md's remote client status. A global collection's `id` is the empty string; the diff runs only on passes that dispatched something; the `runs` collection waits for its endpoint.* Acceptance: the timer refresh of A2 is gone and every host-side change reaches the client within a pass; the mutation-between-hello-and-snapshot test passes on both sides.
501:- The subscriber queue overflows: `resync_required`, the socket closes, the host's frame loop and a second subscriber are unaffected (spike and adapter test).
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, Hash)]
pub struct Rect {
    pub x: u32,
    pub y: u32,
    pub w: u32,
    pub h: u32,
}

/// What kind of record an id names.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
#[serde(rename_all = "kebab-case")]
pub enum RecordKind {
    Project,
    Session,
    Space,
    Set,
    Run,
}

/// One record a command made.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct Made {
    pub kind: RecordKind,
    pub id: String,
}

/// Whether the pane exists and what it is doing.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, Hash)]
#[serde(rename_all = "kebab-case")]
pub enum Liveness {
    Running,
    Exited { code: Option<i32> },
    Missing,
}

/// One session as the port reports it.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, Hash)]
pub struct SessionView {
    pub id: String,
    pub project: String,
    pub name: String,
    pub kind: SessionKind,
    pub cwd: PathBuf,
    pub notes: String,
    pub liveness: Liveness,
    /// The card's word: `CARD_WORKING`, `CARD_IDLE`, "waiting on you", ...
    pub card: String,
    pub last_exit: Option<i32>,
    /// When the agent last reported that it finished a turn (Claude
    /// Code's Stop hook), in milliseconds since the epoch.
    pub last_stop_at_ms: Option<u64>,
    /// How long the pane has printed nothing, when it is running.
    pub quiet_secs: Option<u64>,
    /// When the pane last printed, in milliseconds since the epoch, for
    /// a client that derives quiet itself. An older app omits it.
    #[serde(default)]
    pub last_activity_ms: Option<u64>,
    pub waiting: bool,
    pub waiting_reason: Option<String>,
    /// The pane shows Claude Code's own folder trust question, which
    /// comes before any hook and which `session.trust` answers.
    #[serde(default)]
    pub trust_question: bool,
    /// Why a `session.prompt` now would be refused, or `None` when it
    /// would type. An older app omits it.
    #[serde(default)]
    pub prompt_refusal: Option<String>,
    /// The provider's session id, once the agent has one.
    pub resume_id: Option<String>,
    pub op: Option<String>,
    /// What the agent's last Stop listed as still in flight: background
    /// task kinds (`shell`, `subagent general-purpose`), then `wakeup` or
    /// `recurring wakeup` per cron. Empty from an older app.
    #[serde(default)]
    pub pending: Vec<String>,
    /// The earliest one-shot wakeup's fire time, in milliseconds since
    /// the epoch.
    #[serde(default)]
    pub wakeup_at_ms: Option<u64>,
    /// Until when the last Stop is not the end of the agent's work: the
    /// wakeup's time plus a grace, or a cap on background work. `None`
    /// when nothing is pending; an older app omits it.
    #[serde(default)]
    pub held_until_ms: Option<u64>,
    /// The agent's transcript file as last seen, for a reader that
    /// counts what the session spent. An older app omits it.
    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
    pub transcript: Option<PathBuf>,
}

